  [
    "Where can I join CAT coaching in Chennai?",
    "EduShastra runs weekday and weekend CAT batches at Guru Nanak College, Anna Garden, Velachery, Chennai, Tamil Nadu-600042. You can also study the same course live online from home anywhere in Chennai."
  ],
  [
    "Should I choose classroom CAT coaching or online CAT coaching from Chennai?",
    "Online saves commute time and follows the same four-phase course with the same teachers. Choose the Velachery classroom if you prefer studying in person. Pick whichever fits your routine."
  ],
  [
    "Can working professionals in Chennai prepare for CAT with EduShastra?",
    "Yes. Batches run on weekdays and weekends, in the morning or evening, depending on the centre, and live online classes let you study from home. Ask for current batch options."
  ],
  [
    "What is EduShastra's Entrance Mapping Test?",
    "The Mapping Test is an IQ-based (not knowledge-based) test used to segment students into one of five percentile groups. No preparation is required. It measures innate aptitude so we can place you in the batch that matches your current ability."
  ],
  [
    "What is the Apex-25 batch and how is it different from Elite batches?",
    "Apex-25 batches have a maximum of 25 students (vs. 150+ in Elite). Each Apex batch has 8-9 dedicated teachers, creating a 1:3 teacher-student ratio. Admission is through a merit-based Entrance Mapping Test."
  ],
  [
    "What does 'Lifetime Validity' mean?",
    "Once enrolled in an Apex-25 batch, you can retake the full course (all classes, tests and sessions) as many times as needed at zero additional cost. The goal is to ensure you hit your target percentile, not just complete a course."
  ],
  [
    "How does the +99%ile or fee refund promise work?",
    "If you complete the full course requirements and don't achieve the guaranteed percentile for your batch series, you receive a full fee refund. Read the full terms on the Money-Back Promise page before you enroll."
  ],
